\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li720\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  \cf0  Abide with me: fast falls the eventide;
\par \pard\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj The darkness deepens; Lord, with me abide:
\par When other helpers fail, and comforts flee,
\par Help of the helpless, O abide with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Swift to its close ebbs out life's little day;
\par \pard\li720\sl190\slmult0 Earth's joys grow dim, its glories pass away;
\par Change and decay in all around I see:
\par \pard\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj O Thou who changest not, abide with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   I need Thy presence every passing hour;
\par \pard\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj What but Thy grace can foil the tempter's power?
\par Who like Thyself my guide and stay can be?
\par Through cloud and sunshine, O abide with me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   I fear no foe, with Thee at hand to bless;
\par \pard\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj Ills have no weight and tears no bitterness:
\par Where is death's sting? Where, grave, thy victory?
\par I triumph still if thou abide with me.
\par 
\par \pard\li288\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 5. \tab Hold Thou Thy cross before my closing eyes,
\par \pard\li720\sl190\slmult0\qj Shine through the gloom, and point me to the skies;
\par Heaven's morning breaks, and earth's vain shadows flee:
\par \pard          In life, in death, O Lord, abide with   me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

